{
  "requirement": "The SDK interns the node data returned by `Domain::source_node` for the `OutlineData`. `Domain::node_content` returns that node’s contents. Mapping and read failures return errors. Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement gives four obligations. The reviewed tests cover each one.\n\n1. **Interning the node data from `Domain::source_node`.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` reads a supported `OutlineData`. It asserts that the recorded dependency is `Dependency::Node(domain.cache().intern_node(\"source-node\"), returned.fingerprint())`. So the node mapped by `source_node` is interned and used as the dependency.\n\n2. **`Domain::node_content` returns that node's contents.** The same test asserts that `returned.format()` is `\"prepared contents\"`. It asserts that the domain's `read_nodes` equal `[\"source-node\", \"source-node\"]`, so `node_content` is called with the mapped node. It also changes the domain text and asserts that the record is no longer current. That shows the delivered contents are the ones read through the domain. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` asserts that reading a listed node returns `\"a source snapshot\"` and not the on-disk contents.\n\n3. **Mapping and read failures return errors.**\n   - Mapping failures: the direct-read test uses an unknown path (`unknown.txt`) and an unknown selector (`line[unknown]`). Both must return an error containing \"unsupported source item\", add no dependencies, and make no `node_content` read (`reads == 0`).\n   - Read failures: with `fail_read` set, the read must return an error containing \"prepared source read failed\", and no dependency is recorded.\n   - Unknown node references: the configured-agent test sends `read_node` with `{\"node\":\"unknown\"}`. It asserts that the delivered output contains \"invalid node ID\".\n\n4. **Agents use the node reference from discovery with `read_node`.** The configured-agent test drives a mock model through `list_sources`. It passes the listed entry's node to `read_node` and asserts the returned text. It also takes a node from a `search_text` hit and passes it to `read_node`. It asserts that the read's dependencies, input counts, and domain-recorded reads match. Each execution is run twice.\n\nThe remaining marked tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` and the search-redaction test (`search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging`, `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs`) reinforce this: discovery adds no dependency, and only delivered reads do. They do not leave any obligation uncovered, and nothing in the requirement needs more than these tests provide. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
